                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "You get tricked into taking a job as an unpaid backstage intern for a game that literally breaks down while you're playing it, leaving you frantically pulling levers and tossing tape cassettes behind the scenes so the next player doesn't realize the entire production is on fire. It is 15 minutes of puremeta comedic chaos created by the Stanley Parable director, where the actual heist is trying to keep the game engine from collapsing while a voice actor panics in your ear. Playing it for 57 hours is the ultimate power move.",
